    "## 1. Theoretical Foundations: Skip-gram vs. GloVe\n",
    "\n",
    "Word representations have evolved from discrete sparse one-hot encodings to continuous dense distributed representations capturing latent semantics. This study compares two seminal paradigms:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 Word2Vec Skip-gram with Negative Sampling (SGNS)\n",
    "Proposed by Mikolov et al. (2013), Skip-gram is a **local predictive neural model**. Given a sequence of training words $w_1, w_2, \\dots, w_T$, the objective is to maximize the average log probability of predicting context words $w_{t+j}$ within a sliding window $c$ given center word $w_t$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{SG}} = \\frac{1}{T} \\sum_{t=1}^T \\sum_{-c \\le j \\le c, j \\ne 0} \\log P(w_{t+j} \\mid w_t)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Using **Negative Sampling (SGNS)** to approximate the intractable softmax over the full vocabulary $\\mathcal{V}$, the per-pair objective becomes:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{SGNS}} = \\log \\sigma(v'_{w_O}{}^\\top v_{w_I}) + \\sum_{k=1}^K \\mathbb{E}_{w_i \\sim P_n(w)} \\left[ \\log \\sigma(-v'_{w_i}{}^\\top v_{w_I}) \\right]$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $v_w, v'_w \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ denote the target and context embedding vectors, $\\sigma(z) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-z}}$, and $P_n(w) \\propto U(w)^{3/4}$ is the unigram noise distribution raised to the $3/4$ power.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.2 GloVe (Global Vectors for Word Representation)\n",
    "Proposed by Pennington et al. (2014), GloVe bridges the gap between global matrix factorization (like LSA) and local context window methods. It operates on the **global word-word co-occurrence matrix** $X$, where $X_{ij}$ counts how often word $j$ appears in the context of word $i$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The core insight is that the ratio of co-occurrence probabilities of two words with a probe word $k$, $\\frac{P_{ik}}{P_{jk}}$, encodes semantic meaning. GloVe fits a log-bilinear model to these ratios via weighted least squares regression:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{J}_{\\text{GloVe}} = \\sum_{i,j=1}^{|\\mathcal{V}|} f(X_{ij}) \\left( w_i^\\top \\tilde{w}_j + b_i + \\tilde{b}_j - \\log X_{ij} \\right)^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where the weighting function $f(X_{ij}) = \\min\\left(1, \\left(\\frac{X_{ij}}{x_{\\max}}\\right)^\\alpha\\right)$ (typically $\\alpha=0.75, x_{\\max}=100$) prevents rare co-occurrences and extremely frequent stop words from dominating the objective."
   ]
  },
