    "### 2.1 Preprocessing Pipeline Rationale: Lemmatization vs. Stemming\n",
    "\n",
    "Text normalization is critical when training distributed representations. In this pipeline:\n",
    "1. **Lowercasing:** Collapses case variations (e.g., `Government` $\\to$ `government`) to ensure unified vocabulary indices.\n",
    "2. **URL, Punctuation, and Digit Stripping:** Removes non-alphabetic tokens that act as noise in co-occurrence matrices and context windows.\n",
    "3. **Stopword & Short Token Removal:** High-frequency functional words (e.g., `the`, `is`, `which`) dominate context windows without conveying domain semantics; tokens with $\\le 2$ characters are discarded.\n",
    "4. **Lemmatization (WordNetLemmatizer) vs. Stemming:**\n",
    "   - **Stemming (e.g., Porter, Snowball):** Uses rule-based heuristic suffix slicing. It frequently generates non-words (e.g., `economy` $\\to$ `economi`, `business` $\\to$ `busi`, `minister` $\\to$ `minist`) and suffers from **over-stemming** (collapsing distinct words like `universal` and `university` to `univers`) or **under-stemming** (failing to conflate `alumnus` and `alumni`).\n",
    "   - **Lemmatization:** Performs genuine morphological analysis using the Princeton WordNet lexical database. It reduces inflected variants to canonical dictionary headwords (**lemmas**) (e.g., `companies` $\\to$ `company`, `better` $\\to$ `good` with POS, `matches` $\\to$ `match`).\n",
    "   - **Why Lemmatization is Essential for Word Embeddings:** Pre-trained embeddings like GloVe are indexed by true English vocabulary entries. Stemmed pseudo-tokens (`economi`, `technolog`) produce immediate Out-of-Vocabulary (OOV) misses in GloVe, destroying cross-model comparability. Lemmatization preserves linguistic integrity and lexical validity."
   ]
  },
