    "## 3. Word Embedding Models: Skip-gram vs. GloVe\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, we instantiate two continuous vector spaces of identical dimensionality ($d = 100$):\n",
    "1. **Word2Vec Skip-gram (`sg=1`):**\n",
    "   - **Vector Size:** $100$\n",
    "   - **Window Size:** $5$ (symmetric window of 5 words to the left and 5 words to the right)\n",
    "   - **Minimum Count (`min_count`):** $3$ (prunes rare hapax legomena and typos)\n",
    "   - **Training Scheme:** Skip-gram architecture (`sg=1`) optimized via negative sampling ($K=5$) over $15$ epochs directly on the preprocessed BBC corpus.\n",
    "2. **GloVe (`glove-wiki-gigaword-100`):**\n",
    "   - **Vector Size:** $100$\n",
    "   - **Pretraining Source:** Wikipedia 2014 + Gigaword 5 (6 Billion tokens, 400,000 uncased vocabulary).\n",
    "   - **Architecture:** Log-bilinear co-occurrence matrix regression."
   ]
