    "## 5. Dimensionality Reduction & Visualization (PCA vs. t-SNE)\n",
    "\n",
    "To understand the global and local geometry of the embedding spaces, we curate **10 representative keywords per domain (50 keywords total)** and project their 100D representations into 2D:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Dimensionality Reduction Techniques:\n",
    "1. **Principal Component Analysis (PCA):**\n",
    "   - A **linear, orthogonal transformation** that finds eigenvectors maximizing the empirical covariance matrix $\\Sigma = \\frac{1}{N} X^\\top X$.\n",
    "   - Preserves global Euclidean variance and broad axes of variation, but is susceptible to the \"crowding problem\" at the origin.\n",
    "2. **t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE):**\n",
    "   - A **non-linear, probabilistic manifold algorithm** (van der Maaten & Hinton, 2008). It converts pairwise Euclidean distances into conditional probabilities representing similarities, minimizing the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence between high-dimensional Gaussian affinities $p_{j|i}$ and low-dimensional Student-t affinities $q_{ij}$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$KL(P \\parallel Q) = \\sum_{i \\ne j} p_{ij} \\log \\frac{p_{ij}}{q_{ij}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "   - Employs heavy-tailed Student-t distribution in the low-dimensional space to resolve the crowding problem, mapping local semantic neighborhoods into distinct spatial islands."
   ]
  },
