    "## 6. Downstream Task Evaluation: Document Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.1 Document Representation via Centroid Pooling\n",
    "To evaluate the practical utility of the embeddings for document-level understanding, each document $d = (w_1, w_2, \\dots, w_M)$ is mapped to a single 100D feature vector via **mean pooling (centroid embedding)**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$v_d = \\frac{1}{|d \\cap \\mathcal{V}|} \\sum_{w \\in d \\cap \\mathcal{V}} v_w$$\n",
    "\n",
    "If a document contains zero vocabulary words (an empty intersection), it falls back to a 100-dimensional zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.2 Experimental Setup\n",
    "- **Data Partition:** 80% Training ($n=1,780$), 20% Test ($n=445$), stratified across the 5 domains.\n",
    "- **Classifiers:**\n",
    "  1. **Multinomial Logistic Regression:** Convex linear classifier optimizing cross-entropy with L2 regularization ($C=1.0$).\n",
    "  2. **Linear Support Vector Classifier (LinearSVC):** Maximum-margin linear hyperplane separator optimizing the hinge loss."
   ]
